Z||000002||SloPonti||01-07-2000||01:39 AM||||i talked to the guy selling these and he says he has not put them on a fiero yet but he says all the gm cars he has put them on is a good mod! he says the light comes around the gauges and not actually through them he said at least on the camaros! which i think is true because i just sold a 145 speedo out of a z28 and it did not have any holes in it for lights! he is currently taking a picture of his mustang with the lights on and is going to send it to me! if i get it i will give it to you guys if you want it! do you guys think this will work? and what about his speedo recalibration thing? i don't know about this! how does yours work superx!!!! i need info on your gauges! how do they work! also will you be making on to fit the 85 speedo!!!<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000003||superXmotorsports||01-07-2000||09:02 AM||||Hi again.  If you have a backlit gauge and you cover it up with a sticker, not much light will show around the side because it's not designed to work that way.  The gauges I carry are stamped out on a translucent material (red, green, blue etc) and are made the exact same way the factory faces are which they REPLACE.  I don't think I or anyone else could compete with the price of those, but you get what you pay for.  If you have the 80 (highest numerical indicated) speedo from a 85 GT or 85,86 SE etc and don't want to switch to a 120 - I would need at least 20 people to order to have those custom made.  If you have the 85 (h.n.i.) in a 4 cyl then you have 'reflector' type gauges and those stickers may work for you BUT they read 120 and 240, so you would have to do something about that.  I'm not sure where they are telling you to go to have the speedo re-calibrated - if anyone finds a place they could get plenty of business in this matter.  The 240 MPH speedo looks cool, I agree, but is a little unrealistic even for us with the fastest of Fieros.  In about a month or so I will also have the heater controls face available to match the gauges sets per alot of your requests.   I can assure you that the quality of the sets I'm carrying meet that of the original gauges and appear original (other than color)  Thanks again for everyones time and let me know if there is further questions.  SXM.||||reg||1
